# Fixture script-check registry for tests/suites/checks.sh and the scan.sh
# registry-discovery integration test.  NOT a shipped catalog: docs/DESIGN.md
# §13 step 3+ owns modules/dast/checks.rules for real.  One check per
# --intensity tier, plus one `intrusive` check, so the filter chain's every
# branch (docs/FOUNDATION.md tension 15) has a fixture to exercise it.
#
# EVERY ID HERE IS DELIBERATELY DISTINCT FROM EVERY SHIPPED ONE, because E019
# scopes check-id uniqueness to the whole repository rather than to one file -
# so a fixture that squats on an id a real pack later wants makes that pack
# unlintable.  `DAST-HDR-CSP-01` and `DAST-INJ-SQLI-01` here are already the
# placeholder siblings of the shipped `DAST-HDR-CSP_MISSING-01` and
# `DAST-INJ-SQLI_ERROR-01`; `DAST-AUTHZ-OBJREF-01` was renamed from
# `DAST-AUTHZ-IDOR-01` when DAST-29 landed the real check under that name.
# Renaming an id here costs nothing (this registry emits no finding and reaches
# no `state/`), and rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §9.1.1's "stable forever" rule and
# rules/RETIRED.txt are about SHIPPED check ids, which these are not.  When a
# real check needs one of these names, rename the fixture and its assertions in
# tests/suites/checks.sh - do not contort the shipped id.

id: DAST-HDR-CSP-01
title: Content-Security-Policy header missing or unsafe
script: passive/headers.sh
severity: medium
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-1021
owasp: A05:2021
tags: passive
tags: quick
coverage-scope: target
remediation: Set a restrictive Content-Security-Policy header with no unsafe-inline
  or unsafe-eval source, and no wildcard host.
references: CWE-1021

id: DAST-HDR-HSTS-01
title: Strict-Transport-Security header missing or too short
script: passive/headers.sh
severity: low
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-319
owasp: A05:2021
tags: passive
coverage-scope: target
remediation: Set Strict-Transport-Security with a max-age of at least one year
  and includeSubDomains.
references: CWE-319

id: DAST-AUTHZ-OBJREF-01
title: Cross-user object reference not enforced
script: safe-active/authz.sh
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-639
owasp: A01:2021
tags: safe-active
tags: compliance
coverage-scope: target
requires-identities: 2
cis: 6.1
remediation: Enforce an ownership check on every object reference, keyed to the
  authenticated identity rather than a client-supplied id.
references: CWE-639

id: DAST-INJ-SQLI-01
title: SQL injection via request parameter
script: active/sqli.sh
severity: critical
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-89
owasp: A03:2021
tags: active
tags: intrusive
coverage-scope: target
remediation: Use parameterised queries or an ORM that never interpolates
  request-derived data into SQL text.
references: CWE-89

id: DAST-DISC-CRAWL-01
title: Discovery input reachable
script: config-read/discovery.sh
severity: info
confidence: high
cwe: none
owasp: none
tags: config-read
tags: quick
coverage-scope: target
remediation: No fix required; this is a coverage/discovery fact, not a
  vulnerability.
